From: rocjitsu vfio-user GPU emulation
Subject: [PATCH] vfu: skip SDMA ring test when fw_version==0

When fw_load_type=0 (direct firmware load without PSP) and no SDMA
firmware is present, adev->sdma.instance[i].fw_version stays 0.  The
SDMA ring test requires the SDMA engine to execute a WRITE_LINEAR packet
which never completes without actual SDMA hardware.

Skip the ring test when fw_version==0 so SDMA hw_init succeeds in a
vfio-user emulation environment where the SDMA engine is not yet
implemented.

Signed-off-by: rocjitsu vfio-user GPU emulation <rocjitsu@example.com>
---
 amd/amdgpu/sdma_v4_4_2.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/amd/amdgpu/sdma_v4_4_2.c b/amd/amdgpu/sdma_v4_4_2.c
index XXXXXXX..YYYYYYY 100644
--- a/amd/amdgpu/sdma_v4_4_2.c
+++ b/amd/amdgpu/sdma_v4_4_2.c
@@ -1058,6 +1058,10 @@ static int sdma_v4_4_2_ring_test_ring(struct amdgpu_ring *ring)
 {
 	struct amdgpu_device *adev = ring->adev;
 	unsigned i;
+
+	/* Skip ring test when SDMA firmware is not loaded (vfio-user emulation). */
+	if (adev->sdma.instance[ring->me].fw_version == 0)
+		return 0;
+
 	unsigned index;
 	int r;
 	u32 tmp;
